; error: 11:17: 'rows' is given what fixed 'xs' owns, and nothing changes through what a fixed name owns; give it a copy: 'xs.copy() at r'
; A slice of one value repeated holds that value as it is, so each item is
; what the fixed name owns; a slice made of another, or of an array, is a copy
; of its own, at every depth.

task main()
    region r default
    fixed xs = [1, 2, ...]
    fixed pair = [xs, xs]
    flex copied = new [[int]](pair) at r
    flex rows = new [[int]]([xs#2]) at r
    show(copied, rows)
fi
